course: dictionary
lesson: 2626
title: One word, many meanings: design
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Design can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone» uses design as a verb: to plan and draw how something will be made.
explain: Look at the words around design. In «a flower design», it is a noun: a pattern of lines, shapes and colours that decorates something. In «design and technology», it is a school subject where pupils plan and make things.
explain: «By design» means on purpose. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
fact: Design can be a noun: a drawing or plan, or a pattern of lines, shapes and colours.
fact: Design can be a verb: to plan and draw how something will be made or work.
fact: «By design» means on purpose.
fact: «An early flush toilet was designed in England in 1596 by John Harington.» Here designed is a verb.
fact: «Some design stories grow bigger than the truth, so it is worth checking what the designer actually said.»
exercise: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» In this sentence, what does designed mean? | Painted in one colour | Broken into pieces | Bought from a shop | *Planned and drawn out for how it would be made
exercise: «Her bag had a flower design on the front.» What is a design here? | A kind of bag made of cloth | A flower that grows in gardens | *A pattern of lines, shapes and colours
exercise: Sam says, «I left the window open by design, so the room would cool down.» What does by design mean? | In a hurry | *On purpose | By accident | Without any reason
test: «Ella said she would design a new poster for the school trip.» What does design mean here? | To read the poster quietly | *To plan and draw how the poster will look | To throw the poster away | To paint the walls of the hall
test: In «Her design won a prize», what kind of word is design? | *A noun | An adjective | A verb | A full stop
exam: «Some design stories grow bigger than the truth, so it is worth checking what the designer actually said.» What is the best reason to check? | Because the story is too short | *Because the story may be bigger than the truth | Because design is a hard word to spell | Because designers always lie
